## Known limitations

- Labels for the Nordeste include drought-driven renegotiations recorded as
  defaults (label bias). The model learns this pattern; reweighing reduces but
  does not remove it. Correcting labels at the source is the real fix.
- `credit_history_months` under-records history for women whose credit was
  registered under a spouse (measurement bias).
- Group metrics are estimated on finite samples; small groups have wide
  uncertainty even when they pass `min_group_size`.
- Climate shocks outside the training window (e.g. a severe El Niño year) can
  invalidate the model quickly; drift monitoring is the early warning, not a fix.

## Human oversight

- Every flagged application is reviewed by a credit analyst, who can override the
  score and must record a reason.
- Promotion to `champion` in production requires a named approver after reading
  this card; the gate result alone is necessary but not sufficient.
- Override rates and fairness metrics by region, gender, and farm-size band are
  monitored on the inference table; sustained divergence triggers a model review.
